      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in PMR:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " sarilumab (IL-6 inhibitor) for inadeq response to corticosteroids or inability to tolerate a dose ↓; TNF inhibitors (infliximab, adalimumab) haven't shown benefit."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) dose, polymyalgia rheumatica (PMR):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " PMR: 200 mg SC once every two wks in combo w a tapering course of systemic corticosteroids; may be used as monotx following discontinuation of corticosteroids."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ↑ risk of serious infect that may lead to hsp or death; opportunistic infect also reported; ⍉use in pts w an active infect. Prior to starting KEVZARA, test for latent TB; if (+), start tx for TB."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " known hypersensitivity to sarilumab or any of the inactive ingredients."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) neutropenia/CBC screening:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉ initiate KEVZARA in pts w ANC < 2,000/mm3, PLT < 150,000/mm3, or liver transaminases above 1.5 × ULN. Assess ANC prior to initiation and monitor 4 to 8 wks after start of therapy and every 3 mo thereafter. D/c KEVZARA in PMR pts who develop neutropenia (ANC below 1,000 per mm3 @ the end of the dosing interval), thrombocytopenia (PLT below 100,000 per mm3), or AST or ALT elevations 3 × above the ULN."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) LFT monitoring:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Assess ALT and AST prior to initiation and monitor 4 to 8 wks after start of therapy and every 3 mo thereafter; when clinically indicated, consider other LFTs such as bili."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) GI perf:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " GI perforations reported, primarily as comp of diverticulitis; risk may be ↑ w concurrent diverticulitis or concomitant NSAIDs or corticosteroids; promptly evaluate pts presenting w new onset abd Sx."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) live vax:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉ concurrent use of live vax during tx w KEVZARA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sarilumab (Kevzara) CYP substrates:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Blockade of IL-6 signaling by IL-6Rα antagonists such as KEVZARA might reverse the inhibitory effect of IL-6 and restore CYP activity, leading to altered drug concentrations. On initiation or discontinuation of KEVZARA, perform therapeutic monitoring of effect (ex, warfarin) or drug concentration (ex, theophylline) and adjust the dose prn. Exercise caution when co-administering KEVZARA w CYP3A4 substrate drugs where ↓ in effectiveness = undesirable, ex, PO contraceptives, lovastatin, atorvastatin."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
